 <div id="taskChecklist"></div>
 </article>
 
 <!-- The Real-World JavaScript Problem -->
 <article class="concept-card" style="background: #fff7ed; border-left: 4px solid #f97316;">
 <h3 style="color: #c2410c;"><span></span> The Real-World JavaScript Problem</h3>
 <p style="color: #9a3412; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">Without generics, you either have to duplicate code 50 times (`getUserResponse`, `getProductResponse`, `getOrderResponse`) or use `data: any`, which turns off all autocomplete and type safety in your frontend.</p>
 </article>

 <!-- Core Concept & Analogy -->
 <article class="concept-card">
 <h3><span></span> Core Architecture &amp; Mental Model</h3>
 <div class="analogy-callout">
 <strong>Real-World Analogy:</strong> A Generic `&lt;T&gt;` is like a transparent glass label on a moving box. When you build the box, it says `&lt;T&gt;`. When you fill it with Books, the label morphs into `Box&lt;Book&gt;`, and your editor knows every book has a `.title`.
 </div>
 </article>

 <!-- Syntax & Anatomy Breakdown -->
 <article class="concept-card">
 <h3><span></span> Syntax &amp; Anatomy Breakdown</h3>
 <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #334155; line-height: 1.7;">
 <code>function identity&lt;T&gt;(value: T): T &#123; return value; &#125;</code><br/>
• <strong>&lt;T&gt;</strong> → Declares the type placeholder<br/>
• <strong>value: T</strong> → Whatever type is passed in becomes the type of <code>value</code><br/>
• <strong>: T</strong> → Guarantees the exact same type is returned
 </div>
 </article>

 <!-- The VS Code Beginner Trap -->
 <article class="concept-card" style="background: #fef2f2; border-left: 4px solid #ef4444;">
 <h3 style="color: #b91c1c;"><span>️</span> The VS Code Beginner Trap (What NOT to do)</h3>
 <p style="color: #991b1b; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">By convention, single capital letters are used for generics: `T` (Type), `K` (Key), `V` (Value), `E` (Element). Don't use confusing names like `&lt;MySpecialVariable&gt;`.</p>
 </article>

 <!-- Reference Pattern / Starter Code -->
 <article class="concept-card">
